summary:
All dev fixtures now pass: the final verify reports **1013 of 1013 fixtures pass (dev)**, up from 994 at the start. `npm run check` passes.

**What changed**
- **Classic credits (DSC-04).** In classic mode the unused-time credit now applies every discount that was on the item's billed line, including ones whose share of the invoice was 0. The previous pass dropped those, and nothing in dev could catch it.
- **New item at 0 (PRO-11).** In classic mode, when the changed item's new amount is 0, the preview no longer has a remaining-time line. The renewal still lists the item at 0. Flexible mode is unchanged.
- **Result of those two.** I predicted all 11 failing dev-b3-classic-* would flip and nothing else would move. That is what happened (1005 of 1013).
- **The agent's API calls.** The dev-ag-* cases compare whole response bodies, so the clone now returns Stripe's full shapes for subscriptions, subscription items, prices, customers, discounts and invoice items. New endpoints:
  - changing items through `POST /v1/subscriptions/:id` and `POST /v1/subscription_items/:id`, which create pending proration items;
  - adding a coupon with `discounts[0][coupon]`;
  - previews that include pending items first;
  - `GET /v1/invoices/upcoming`, which returns the deprecation error;
  - listing a customer's subscriptions, and reading a price, a customer and a subscription's items;
  - expanding discounts when reading a subscription.

  On a flexible subscription the legacy `coupon` parameter is refused, because that is what the recording shows. In a local replay 8 of 9 cases passed first time. The last one failed because the clone did not read the `expand[]=discounts` form; after fixing that, all 7 dev-ag-* and dev-v3-two-subscriptions pass. dev-v3-past-due-recovers already passed.

**Rules I could not make pass:** none in dev. These are implemented without any dev fixture to check them against, so treat them as guesses:
- `always_invoice` on a real update;
- an interval change made for real (cycle reset);
- the legacy `coupon` parameter on a classic subscription;
- the classic `billing_mode` object shape;
- a second change within the same period;
- LIF-03 and LIF-04, which still have no dev fixtures.

**Fixtures that contradict rules.json**
- **DSC-07** still disagrees with dev-t2-c-forever-forever and dev-t2-b-always-flexible-forever, as recorded in pass 4: a single carried forever coupon is listed on the credit line instead of the coupon passed to the preview.
- **Rule tags (not a behaviour contradiction):** dev-ag-reads is tagged ERR-02 but reads no missing object, and dev-ag-downgrade-no-proration is tagged PRO-06 but sends no proration date.

Everything else in the changed rules (DSC-01, DSC-04, DSC-05, PRO-04, INT-01, ITM-01, MOD-01, PRO-11) matches the dev fixtures.

Last line of the final `npm run verify stripe-billing`:
```
1013 of 1013 fixtures pass (dev)
```

Files changed are all in `/work/targets/stripe-billing/clone/`: `billing.ts`, `api.ts`, `objects.ts`, `state.ts`, `life.ts`, `portal.ts` and `NOTES.md` (pass 6 section). I also left a scratch replay script at `/tmp/replay.ts`, outside the repository.

